; C22  Winning 42 pp. 50-51 (W42-p051-a, W42-p051-b)
; Rule, in our words: in a trump set, the opponent holding trumps and sitting
; just after the bidder, void in the suit of the bidder's double, usually
; trumps it, since count may still fall on the trick; the same opponent in the
; last seat trumps only if count is already on it.
; Python gate (pour_setter gate_c22): a setter at either seat, the bidder led a
; non-trump double, the mover is void in its suit and holds two or more trumps;
; the book's tiles are his trumps.
; How this encoding differs: it fires only from the seat after the bidder
; (S1), as the book says; the gate also fires from the last seat, where the
; book's rule depends on the count already played. "Holds two or more trumps"
; is the gate's reading of the book's trump-rich opponent; the book's trigger
; (only one opponent followed the first trump lead) is not written.
; Void in the led suit is read from the hand: a legal trump on a non-trump lead.
; GAP declarer: the bidder is written in as S0, the left seat as S1.
; GAP history, GAP shown-void: the trump-set trigger, as in C14.
(policy c22-trump-the-double-from-the-left
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule trump-in (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (domino doubled) (domino ruff) (domino other) (context led))
        (out ruff)
        (pattern
          (viewer S1)
          (leader S0)
          (trick-play S0 doubled)
          (double doubled)
          (not (in doubled q*))
          (led-context led)
          (own-legal ruff)
          (in ruff q*)
          (own-legal other)
          (in other q*))))))
